 6. Quick hits 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 A U.S. Air Force KC-46A Pegasus, flown by the 141st Air Refueling Squadron. Photo: Michael Hong/DVIDS

 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 🇶🇦 The State Department approved a potential sale of Boeing-made KC-46As and related equipment to Qatar for $4.5 billion.

 Why it matters: The notification describes Qatar, which last year secured a diet version of Article 5 with the U.S., as "an important force for political stability and economic progress in the Middle East." 💭 My thought bubble: Yes, price tags can change during negotiations. But it's a huge commitment, either way. 🌌 Muon Space raised $250 million. The Series C was led by Eclipse Capital. Other participants included Galvanize, Salesforce Ventures and Woven Capital.

 Why it matters: "Space infrastructure needs to scale the way cloud infrastructure did," CEO Jonny Dyer said in a statement. 💭 My thought bubble: Is space the new drones? (Not bait, I swear.) 🪖 Gen. Christopher LaNeve, the Army vice chief of staff, published his vision for the service, which states that a "secure Western Hemisphere is a prerequisite for joint power projection" and that the "next war will not look like our last."

 Why it matters: "Gen. LaNeve is releasing his azimuth now because soldiers deserve to know how the Army fights and what's expected of them," Maj. Peter Sulzona, a spokesperson, told me. 💭 My thought bubble: Have you read the Wall Street Journal exclusive ? Thoughts? 💥 Hanwha Defense USA plans to deliver its first Mobile Tactical Cannon prototype to the Army this fall.

 Why it matters: It's HDUSA's first major contract with the service — and it's on a speedy schedule. (Hanwha has 2,500-plus K9 howitzers fielded globally.) 💭 My thought bubble: The Army has been exploring M777 replacements for years now. We'll see what sticks. 
 
